# funr2_rush.dem — pp-playtest-fun R2, strategy 1: RUSH.
# Doctrine (declared up front, round-1 comparable): blanket standard mesh as
# fast as the Box allows, 4 routers pre-placed, ZERO fiber pre-investment;
# react to era-3 with a steady grind — 1 wide per 2 s, trunk-first, starting
# at 32 s (2 s after the gate fires at tick 600). Grind completes at 56 s —
# ~26 s into the 45 s grace. Question: does reactive-but-unhurried play now
# survive the arrival AND carry the surge?
seed 2026
run 152000ms
era 2
health on
win surge 90
box on
advance gate on
fixture off
spawn_node residential 4 10
spawn_node residential 4 22
spawn_node residential 12 8
spawn_node residential 14 24
spawn_node residential 18 8
spawn_node residential 20 24
spawn_node residential 26 8
spawn_node residential 30 24
spawn_node small_biz 36 20
spawn_node content_host 36 26
spawn_node router_basic 8 16
spawn_node router_basic 16 16
spawn_node router_basic 24 16
spawn_node router_basic 32 16
at 100ms draw 0 10 standard
at 100ms draw 1 10 standard
at 100ms draw 2 10 standard
at 100ms draw 3 11 standard
at 100ms draw 4 11 standard
at 100ms draw 10 11 standard
at 100ms draw 5 12 standard
at 100ms draw 6 12 standard
at 100ms draw 11 12 standard
at 100ms draw 7 13 standard
at 100ms draw 8 13 standard
at 100ms draw 9 13 standard
at 100ms draw 12 13 standard
# the reactive grind: trunk first, then feeders — 1 wide / 2 s
at 32000ms modernize 5 wide
at 34000ms modernize 8 wide
at 36000ms modernize 11 wide
at 38000ms modernize 0 wide
at 40000ms modernize 1 wide
at 42000ms modernize 2 wide
at 44000ms modernize 3 wide
at 46000ms modernize 4 wide
at 48000ms modernize 6 wide
at 50000ms modernize 7 wide
at 52000ms modernize 9 wide
at 54000ms modernize 10 wide
at 56000ms modernize 12 wide
capture at 32000ms
capture at 40000ms
capture at 60000ms
capture at 75000ms
expect hash stable
